+<h4>List.code with a local code</h4>
+<p>
+For example, <a href="list-definitions.html#List.code">List.code</a> has an example binding. An implementation can use
+a code from another code system when the illustrative value set does not include the concept it needs to communicate:
+</p>
+
+<pre class="json">
+{
+  "resourceType": "List",
+  "status": "current",
+  "mode": "working",
+  "code": {
+    "coding": [
+      {
+        "system": "http://example.org/fhir/CodeSystem/list-purpose",
+        "code": "care-team-tasks",
+        "display": "Care team tasks"
+      }
+    ],
+    "text": "Care team tasks"
+  }
+}
+</pre>
+<p>
+This is conformant because example bindings are illustrative, not restrictive. Receivers should not assume that the
+codes in an example value set are complete or production ready.
+</p>
